%% Digital Twin - sequence: how machine state is derived, not read live
%% Sources: apps/web/src/routes/_authenticated/dashboard.tsx (parallel twin fetch),
%%          apps/api/src/index.ts (/api/twin, /api/report/live, resolveReportScope),
%%          apps/api/src/report/clickhouse-report.ts (queryMachineStates, buildMachineStateSQL,
%%          buildBranchHoursSQL, queryBranchHours, usageFreshnessOf, resolveBranchOpenState),
%%          apps/web/src/lib/branch-availability-view.ts (effectiveAvailability),
%%          apps/web/src/lib/machine-status.ts (freshnessMeta, branchOpenStateMeta)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Exec as Executive (owner)
    participant Web as Web dashboard
    participant API as LaundryTwin API
    participant Guard as Access guard
    participant CH as ClickHouse
    participant Dwh as Warehouse tables

    Note over Exec,Dwh: 1. The twin is requested with the dashboard

    Exec->>Web: opens /dashboard (twin card is on the same page)
    Web->>+API: GET /api/twin?from&to (no branchId for an owner)
    API->>Guard: requireReportPrincipal + resolveReportScope
    Guard-->>API: owner, so scope = undefined (all branches)

    Note over API,Dwh: 2. Two independent queries, deliberately not joined

    par Machine state
        API->>+CH: buildMachineStateSQL(from, to, branchId = '')
        CH->>Dwh: dim_machine FINAL JOIN dim_branch FINAL<br/>LEFT JOIN fact_machine_usage FINAL
        Note over CH: argMax(status, started_at) = latest status<br/>max(started_at) = last activity<br/>countIf(status IN paid, finished) = cycle count
        Dwh-->>CH: one row per machine
        CH-->>-API: rows
    and Opening hours (best effort)
        API->>+CH: buildBranchHoursSQL(branchId)
        Note over API,CH: a SEPARATE query on purpose: dim_branch_hours<br/>does not exist on every warehouse, and a JOIN would fail<br/>the whole machine query with Code 60 UNKNOWN_TABLE
        alt table exists
            CH->>Dwh: dim_branch_hours FINAL
            Dwh-->>CH: open_minute / close_minute / open_days
            CH-->>API: hours
        else table missing or query fails
            CH-->>API: empty map (no schedule)
            Note over API,CH: failure degrades to "unknown" schedule,<br/>it never fails the twin
        end
        deactivate CH
    end

    Note over API,Dwh: 3. Three states, never collapsed into two

    API->>API: usageFreshnessOf(lastActiveAt)<br/>fresh (<= 30 min) / stale / unavailable
    API->>API: resolveBranchOpenState(hours, timezone, now)<br/>open / closed / unknown
    API->>API: hasUsageRows = usage_rows > 0

    alt machine has usage rows
        API->>API: cycleCount = counted cycles<br/>cycleCountSource = "usage_row"
        Note over API: a real 0 stays a real 0
    else no usage rows in the window
        API->>API: cycleCount = null<br/>cycleCountSource = "unavailable"
        Note over API: null is "not measured",<br/>never "measured zero"
    end

    API-->>-Web: 200 machines[], availability = usage-derived
    Note over API,Web: source = clickhouse, and fetchedAt is stamped

    Note over Web,Dwh: 4. The web decides what may be claimed

    Web->>Web: freshnessMeta(freshness) -> Thai label
    Web->>Web: effectiveAvailability(freshness, branchOpenState)

    alt branch positively closed
        Note over Web: render "closed according to opening hours"<br/>in a neutral pill, not red
    else branch open, or schedule unknown
        Note over Web: pass freshness through UNCHANGED -<br/>an unknown schedule must not suppress a real fault
    end

    Web-->>Exec: twin grid: status, freshness, cycle count + basis

    Note over Exec,Dwh: 5. What the twin is NOT

    Note over Exec,Dwh: fact_machine_event holds 0 rows (measured on the VM),<br/>so no live telemetry exists. Twin state is DERIVED from usage rows.
    Note over Exec,Dwh: /api/report/events answers availability = "unavailable"<br/>with a reason, because an empty list would read as "no events happened".

    alt analytics source unreachable
        API-->>Web: 503 ANALYTICS_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
        Web-->>Exec: Thai message naming the source
    end
